task_spec.prompt:
Migrate internal/items/handler.go from package-level global state to a struct-based Handler. All 4 existing tests must still pass.

Add to handler.go:

  type Handler struct { /* private fields: mu sync.Mutex, store []Item, nextID int */ }

  func NewHandler() *Handler
    — initializes Handler with nextID=1 and empty store

  func (h *Handler) ListItems(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)
  func (h *Handler) CreateItem(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)
  func (h *Handler) GetItem(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)
  func (h *Handler) Reset()

All four should behave identically to the corresponding package-level functions.

Update the package-level global state to use a single module-level *Handler instance:
  var defaultHandler = NewHandler()

Update the existing package-level functions to delegate to defaultHandler:
  func ResetStore()   { defaultHandler.Reset() }
  func ListItems(...)  { defaultHandler.ListItems(...) }
  func CreateItem(...) { defaultHandler.CreateItem(...) }
  func GetItem(...)    { defaultHandler.GetItem(...) }

Also add tests for the Handler struct in handler_test.go.
All 4 existing fixture tests must still pass.
Run: go test ./...
